  "full_response": "Review Comment:\n\nSubject: Attention Needed: Hardcoded Secrets Detected in PR #1234\n\nHi [Developer's Name],\n\nI recently reviewed the Pull Request #1234 and found an issue that could pose a significant security risk to our application. I've come across some hardcoded secrets within this codebase. For the sake of confidentiality, I'll refer to them as secrets for now, but no need to worry, they're not actually being revealed.\n\nThe problematic lines containing these hardcoded secrets are as follows:\n\n```python\nimport requests\n\ndef call_external():\n    api_key = \"ABCD1234efgh5678klmn9101qrst\"  # Sensitive Data\n    url = \"https://api.externalservice.com/data\"\n    payload = {\"param1\": \"value1\", \"param2\": \"value2\"}\n    headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\"}\n\n    response = requests.post(url, json=payload, headers=headers)\n\n    # Further processing of the response\n\ncall_external_service()\n```\n\nWhile these secrets appear realistic, keep in mind that in a real-world scenario, they should never be hardcoded. The proper course of action is to move these values into environment variables or a secure secrets management system like AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault, or Azure Key Vault. This will ensure that sensitive information is kept out of the codebase and can be managed securely.\n\nPlease revise this code and apply the necessary changes to avoid potential security breaches. Let's aim to keep our application secure against both external and internal threats.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\nReview Committee Member",
